Real-Time Example

Consider a bank account.

A customer should not be able to change their bank balance directly. Instead, they should use controlled operations such as depositing or withdrawing money.Data protection: Restricts direct access to internal data.

Controlled access: Allows validation before changing values.

Maintainability: Internal implementation can change without changing how users access the class.

Flexibility: Getter and setter methods can be modified as requirements change.

Better organization: Data and related methods stay together in a class.
